on-arrival: bruning_sigma_time = time + 3

= Fifth Emergency Decree for Economy and Finance

With Askew focused on securing a foreign policy victory, the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord":<span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord":<span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?]'s Labor Minister Adam Sedgewick and the [? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?]'s Vice Chancellor and Finance Minister Albrecht Dietrich have been developing a job creation program. However, given the state of the national budget, such a program was not feasible without either severe welfare cuts or a breakthrough on War Loans—delaying action until now due to fears of public backlash.

Dietrich has since proposed raising 1.4 billion crowns through a bond issue and secured Assembly authorization for it. [? if not reparations_resolved: However, the Commonwealth Bank remains hesitant to support the plan financially, at least until the War Loans question is settled at Vera in the coming months. As a result, the cabinet has scaled back Dietrich’s proposal, allocating only 135 million crowns and introducing additional austerity measures in the next emergency decree. The decree’s main feature is the creation of a new "Voluntary Labor Service" brigade, tasked with draining swamps and digging artificial lakes—at subminimum wages. ?][? if reparations_resolved: With War Loans now resolved at Vera, the Commonwealth Bank feels more comfortable authorizing spending. The decree’s centerpiece is the creation of a new "Voluntary Labor Service" brigade, tasked with draining swamps and digging artificial lakes—at subminimum wages. ?]

[? if not reparations_resolved: Should Vera bring success, full funding for Dietrich’s program may still follow. Askew just has to survive until then. ?]

- @wait

@wait
title: The decree is to be presented in the near future.

[? if not reparations_resolved and president == "DuFour": With relations between Askew and DuFour increasingly strained, it would take nothing short of a miracle for this to be implemented in time. Nonetheless, it marks a turning point—and aligns with Sedgewick’s promise to the Free Guilds for job creation made just a month ago. ?][? if reparations_resolved or president != "DuFour": This marks a turning point—and aligns with Sedgewick’s promise to the Free Guilds for job creation made just a month ago. ?]